      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury count",
          "heading": "Quesada says 17 Italy players are unavailable as captaincy call looms",
          "body": "Gonzalo Quesada says 17 players are unavailable for Italy's autumn Tests, a significant difficulty given they are key figures. Four consecutive matches against top-ten opponents, starting with South Africa in Turin, are among the most demanding in Italy's history, he says. He will decide on the captaincy next week, with Giacomo Nicotera and Niccolò Cannone, both former captains, among the options. Tommaso Allan is under consideration for the 23 but has not yet trained fully, with full training targeted the following week."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Argentina prop Thomas Gallo out at least six months after wrist surgery",
