      "edition": "Friday 30 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Macs Page called into Wales squad after Rio Dyer hamstring withdrawal",
          "body": "Wales have made a late change to their squad for the November Nations Championship, with Dragons wing Rio Dyer released after a hamstring injury suffered in the 31-14 defeat to Ospreys last Saturday. Dyer had only just been recalled. Steve Tandy has called up uncapped Scarlets back Macs Page in his place, Page's first senior call-up since July. He becomes the fourth uncapped player in the extended squad, alongside Rhys Barratt, Che Hope and Aneurin Owen."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Argentina prop Thomas Gallo out at least six months after wrist surgery",
