    "465": {
      "date": "2026-10-30",
      "edition": "Friday 30 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection policy",
          "heading": "NZ Rugby's Steve Lancaster opens door to relaxing All Blacks selection policy",
          "body": "New Zealand Rugby could relax its strict policy on picking All Blacks who do not play for one of the five Super Rugby Pacific clubs, Planet Rugby reports. The union on Thursday backed Super Rugby Pacific and the NPC as the right competitions for the All Blacks, keeping the status quo over a proposal to replace Super Rugby Pacific with an 8-10 team national competition. NZR chief Steve Lancaster's comments hint at a policy shift, with the final Board decision still to come and implementation expected from 2028."
